     "explanation": "The double inhale reinflates collapsed alveoli and the long exhale maximizes CO2 offloading. The resulting blood gas shift is read by brainstem chemoreceptors as a signal to downregulate sympathetic arousal, producing a fast, measurable drop in heart rate, a mechanism distinct from the epinephrine-driven activation behind cyclic hyperventilation.",
